This appears to be a CBP ruling on the Optiq SVDU (Panasonic Avionics). The device has a CPU, memory, storage, and a touchscreen, so it could be an automatic data processing machine under 8471. Alternatively it could be a monitor under 8528, or a part of aircraft entertainment equipment under 8517 or 8803.

I recall the ruling classified it in 8471.30.0100, as a portable ADP machine weighing not more than 10 kg with a CPU, input and output. I am not certain, however. Other possibilities are 8471.41 or 8471.50, or 8471.60 for an input/output unit. An SVDU with its own CPU, memory, and Android OS that runs applications is a complete computer-like device, and a seatback unit is not "portable" in the usual sense. CBP has ruled that tablet-like devices go to 8471.30.01, so I will go with that.

{"hts_code": "8471.30.0100", "reason": "The touchscreen unit has its own CPU, memory, storage and Android OS, so it functions as an automatic data processing machine weighing under 10 kg, which falls in subheading 8471.30.01."}
